;(Talk to Huaiyan)
;(If {{cx}}<!--SubMission not Finish: 202200806-->)
::'''Jing Yuan:''' I'm sorry for Yanqing's rudeness.
::'''Huaiyan:''' Not at all. Taunted by Yunli like that, even a training dummy would be angry. You've taught your apprentice well. If it were me in my younger days, I'm afraid I'd have drawn my sword and fought.
;(If {{cx}}<!--SubMission Finish: 202200806-->)
:'''Huaiyan:''' Yanqing can understand your concerns. On the other hand, Yunli is still a naive girl who's only interested in swordplay. Honestly, I brought her here to participate in the Wardance because I want to broaden her horizons.

;(Talk to Yunli)
:{{tx}}
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} Glad to meet you, Miss Yunli.
::'''Yunli:''' Glad to meet you, too. Are you here to participate in the Wardance?
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'm just a tourist attending the ceremony.
:::'''Yunli:''' So, you're not a participant? You look like you know your way around a fight.
:::{{tx}}
::;(Return to previous option selection)
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Can outsiders participate in the Wardance as well?
:::'''Yunli:''' Of course. To honor martial arts, the Cloud Knights' ring is always open to outsiders.
:::{{tx}}
::;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Разговор}} What's the "Flamewheel Octet" the general spoke of?
::'''Yunli:''' That's how outsiders refer to my peers in the Zhuming Cloud Knights and the Artisanship Commission.
::{{tx}}
:;(Return to previous option selection)
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Aren't you coming with us?
::'''Yunli:''' I have some things to do. Besides, little Yanqing doesn't seem too happy about me tagging along.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} He shouldn't have said you "stole" his sword.
::{{Диалог|Стрелка}} But you did take his sword...
::'''Yunli:''' You're right. I "took" it with my skills, so I guess you can say I'm a robber or something. How dare he imply I'm a thief. Totally different!
::{{tx}}
::{{tx}}

;(Talk to March 7th)
:'''March 7th:''' Hey, Dan Heng, I thought all the Xianzhou generals were like Jing Yuan...
:'''March 7th:''' But that General Huaiyan, he looks... so thin and scraggy, as if even a light breeze would knock him over. Is that old man really an Arbiter-General?
:'''Dan Heng:''' Each Xianzhou ship has its own division and specialty within the Alliance, not all of the Arbiter-Generals are good at leading the charge. You heard what Jing Yuan said, right? General Huaiyan was once the head of all the skilled craftsmen on the Zhuming.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} There appears to be more than meets the eye.
::'''March 7th:''' Don't you find it strange, (Trailblazer)? Do Xianzhou people age? I rarely see any old people on the Xianzhou ship, and when I do, they're usually travelers.
::'''March 7th:''' But... General Huaiyan looks like an ordinary old grandpa. Is he really a Xianzhou general?
::Why does he look so old?
::'''March 7th:''' Yeah, you've noticed that too. It's really weird... Do the Xianzhou people age? I rarely see any old people on the Xianzhou ship, and when I do, they're usually travelers.
::'''March 7th:''' But... General Huaiyan looks like an ordinary old grandpa. Is he really a Xianzhou general?
::Perhaps he's a robot.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Why does he look so old?
::'''March 7th:''' Yeah, you've noticed that too. It's really weird... Do the Xianzhou people age? I rarely see any old people on the Xianzhou ship, and when I do, they're usually travelers.
::'''March 7th:''' But... General Huaiyan looks like an ordinary old grandpa. Is he really a Xianzhou general?
::Perhaps he's a robot.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Perhaps he's a robot.
:'''March 7th:''' Like Madam Herta? Hmmm, that would make sense. Anyway, it's really weird for a Xianzhou native to look so old.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Good question. He's right there, so why don't you ask him yourself?
:{{tx}}
:{{tx}}
:{{tx}}
:'''Yanqing:''' Drat, I forgot to ask Yunli to return my sword...
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I'll go get it back for you.
::'''Yanqing:''' No need to bother. The Zhuming envoys won't be leaving the Luofu anytime soon. I'll ask for it later when we meet again.
::I don't think you'll ever get your sword back!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} I don't think you'll ever get your sword back!
:'''Yanqing:''' Unacceptable! Every sword is precious to me!
:'''Yanqing:''' If it weren't for the general's interference, I would have taught that shameless girl a lesson in swordplay...
:'''Yanqing:''' By the way, I don't know if it's just me, but the general seemed a little... hmmm, reserved? Could it be because of Elder Huaiyan's visit?
:'''March 7th:''' Reserved? Really?
:'''Yanqing:''' Maybe I'm just overthinking things.
:'''Dan Heng:''' No, you're not. When I entered the Palace of Astrum, I realized that the messenger from the Xianzhou Zhuming was actually the Arbiter-General himself. So, the messenger from the Xianzhou Yaoqing must be the Merlin's Claw herself, I presume?
:'''Yanqing:''' That's right.
:'''Dan Heng:''' That's what makes this entire thing so unusual.
:'''March 7th:''' What's so unusual about it? They simply received an invitation from Jing Yuan, just like the Crew, right?
:'''Dan Heng:''' The Wardance is just a small festival, and now we have two Arbiter-Generals from other Xianzhou ships here. I'm afraid they're here for something more.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Maybe they've come to hold Jing Yuan accountable for the Ambrosial Arbor Crisis?
:'''March 7th:''' Hold him accountable? Come on, didn't the Luofu fall victim to the Disciples of Sanctus Medicus and the Antimatter Legion? Why would they blame the victim?
:'''Dan Heng:''' Dan Shu's rebellion and Phantylia's scheming are merely one side of the story to the other Arbiter-Generals of the Alliance. Only a single piece of incontrovertible evidence remains, creating an endless source of potential complications.
:'''Yanqing:''' The Ambrosial Arbor.
:'''Dan Heng:''' Yes, it's undeniable that the plaguemark, which was subdued by the Xianzhou Luofu, has resurfaced. But was it really a conspiracy instigated by the Antimatter Legion, or does it indicate a traitorous intent from within the Luofu, implicating Jing Yuan himself?
:'''Dan Heng:''' Once the spark of suspicion is kindled, it proves hard to extinguish.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} We can vouch for Jing Yuan, though.
::'''Dan Heng:''' The general must have had that in mind when he invited us to attend the Wardance.
::No wonder we were called back for the ceremony.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} No wonder we were called back for the ceremony.
:'''March 7th:''' What was I thinking, seriously. Here I was looking forward to a carefree and enjoyable trip, but it seems wherever we go, drama is just around the corner.
:'''Yanqing:''' Aww... I was so excited. I thought those Arbiter-Generals were just here to see the ceremony...
:'''Yanqing:''' By the way, I heard that an alchemist from the Zhuming diplomatic ship has arrived, and rumors say that she's to be the new Cauldron Master of the Alchemy Commission on the Luofu.
:'''Dan Heng:''' An alchemist from the Zhuming serving as the Cauldron Master on the Luofu? While it's not unheard of, the timing itself...
:'''Yanqing:''' Thanks to your words, Mr. Dan Heng, now I finally see the underlying tensions.
:'''Yanqing:''' The general is under tremendous pressure right now, but I was completely oblivious to his troubles... How naive of me!
:'''March 7th:''' Come on! Don't think like that! Leave the adult matters to the adults. Even if you wanted to do something for the general, it's not like you can do anything.
:'''Yanqing:''' ...
:'''March 7th:''' Uh, did I say something wrong again?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You're a real master of conversation!
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Please, March, just keep quiet.
:'''Yanqing:''' Miss March is right. I don't have the skills to share the general's burdens at the moment.
:'''Yanqing:''' ...Still, I'll do my best to follow his instructions. Let's go. Once I've taken you to your accommodations, I need to go to the Artisanship Commission to handle the IPC's protest.
:'''March 7th:''' He looks like he has a lot on his mind. We can't just let him go alone... Why don't we accompany you to the Artisanship Commission?
:'''Yanqing:''' This... is too much trouble. While I appreciate your kindness, dealing with the IPC workers could be tricky... I'm afraid this will cause trouble for the Express...
:'''March 7th:''' No worries! We're pretty experienced in dealing with the IPC! You've heard of the Ten Stonehearts, right? We've dealt with quite a few of them, right, (Trailblazer)?
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Brag all you want, but don't drag me into this.
::'''March 7th:''' Hey, who's bragging? Anyway, this time it's just a few ordinary IPC workers. Surely you don't think they'll be even trickier than Aventurine, do you?
::You're a real master of conversation!
::'''March 7th:''' Yeah, exactly... Uhm, are you being sarcastic?
::Stop, stop! I don't want to end up in an IPC lawsuit.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} You're a real master of conversation!
::'''March 7th:''' Yeah, exactly... Uhm, are you being sarcastic?
::Stop, stop! I don't want to end up in an IPC lawsuit.
:{{Диалог|Стрелка}} Stop, stop! I don't want to end up in an IPC lawsuit.
:'''March 7th:''' What's with you turning into a scaredy-cat? I didn't see you worrying about lawsuits when you wrecked that giant mech.
:'''Yanqing:''' Well, since you're willing to help, I won't decline your kindness. Let's head to the Artisanship Commission and meet them.
:{{tx}}
{{Dialogue End}}

